.KEY demo/A
.BRA {
.KET }
;
; Run a MesaGL demo with the stack it actually needs.
;
;     Execute S:gl-run gears
;
; The shell gives a command AROS_STACKSIZE, which is 0xA000 -- 40 KB -- on
; m68k. Mesa's initialisation is nowhere near that shallow: on a Raspberry Pi 3
; the demos come up only after `stack 100000000`, and at 1 MB they do not. That
; is not a tuning knob, it is the difference between working and not.
;
; Verified on hardware: with this stack, gl_test creates its context, reports
; GL_RENDERER "VC4 V3D 2.1" and Mesa 20.0.8, and enters its render loop.
;
Stack 100000000
SYS:Extras/Demos/GL/{demo}
